// madc --mcp --project over a single file — the one-TU project (split arc 1C,
// item 16). The runner starts `madc --mcp --project tests/testmcp_project.mad`
// (.flags): the project's TU is the served document, a call's `file` names
// it (as the working directory spells it), a file outside the project is
// refused as error content, and every tool advertises `file`. The server
// claims the project for its life (one owner per project, madc::discovery)
// and gives the claim back at end of input. A single file's project memory
// is memory-only: a record lands (log_head 1) and no <file>.events appears
// beside the source (graph.status's log is ""). ORACLE: the MCP specification
// 2025-06-18 (isError content for a tool's own refusal); the graph results'
// shapes as testmcp_stdio's; madcide's proj_events_path (a change log only
// beside a manifest — the implicit single-file project is memory-only).

long add(long a, long b)
{
    return a + b;
}

int main(void)
{
    return (int)add(2, 3) - 5;
}
